### Framing trees

Should we add? The requirement says trees near spawn/lake must not look like bare telephone poles. Right now no trees within 14 in front/side except behind at 14; the visible trees across the lake will have new shape. The screenshot's side trees at right edge were big leaf masses; ours perhaps similar. But to make the spawn view feel like a forest lakeshore, framing trees help. I think adding 2 side trees is a good enhancement. But the user specifically says "must not block the lake vista" – adding trees near spawn is risky without visual verification. We can place them at 65-75° off-axis and 11-14 blocks away, ensuring corridor check passes. They will appear at the far left/right edges, framing. The main lake center remains open. Tree canopies radius 2 (5 wide) at 12 blocks subtend ~24°, so if center at 70°, edges 58-82°, still outside the 20° corridor; view center clear. Good.

Also one behind the player won't be visible initially.

Let's implement with 2 side trees, using a helper that finds a valid spot near the target angle/distance. We need ensure no blocking: after choosing, check `inViewCorridor` for the tree center and four canopy-edge points at ±2, with maxDist 18; skip if any point is in corridor. That guarantees the canopy doesn't intrude into ±20° of the view. Perfect.

Tree species: use biome from column; if isTreeBiome use it; otherwise choose birch if biome is plains? We can just use BIOME.birch for birch shore, BIOME.forest for plains/forest, taiga for taiga, oak for savanna/swamp. Since spawn biome is birch_forest, birch. Actually mixing oak/birch at lakeshore is vanilla. Alternate: left birch, right oak. But worldgen biome may be birch; planting oak in birch forest is acceptable (vanilla birch forests have only birch mostly). Use birch for both to match. Could choose base on hash: 70% birch. Fine.

